{
  "case": "20-box-reduces-across",
  "description": "The reason boxing is worth having: an agent OUTSIDE a boxed mantle rewrites agents INSIDE it, and no rule reaches in to do it. The world holds a player (boxed) and an `amulet`, and the amulet's principal is wired to box port 1 — which IS the inner shirt's principal, because that is what the interface says port 1 is. After composition they are an ordinary active pair in one net, so `cloth x cloth` annihilate fires by ordinary reduction: both vanish and their aux partners cross-link, which leaves the amulet's `chain` wired to the player's own `skin`. An outside object reached through the boundary and rewired the mantle's interior, using nothing but a wire to a free port. The complementary half is structural and just as important: `p1/voice` is untouched and could not have been touched, because no port of it is in the interface and every other inner port is already wired — encapsulation here is linearity, not a scope check some rule could forget.",
